-<!-- Hero -->
-<section class="sec" style="padding-top:6rem">
-<h1>The Evidence</h1>
-<p class="lead" style="font-size:1rem;color:var(--t)"><span data-stat="stories_total">221</span> multi-session stories across <span data-stat="story_sessions">1,097</span> sessions and <span data-stat="variants">7</span> models. Each story is a 5-session greenfield build — CRUD API, static site generator, or notification service — read through five facets: <strong style="color:var(--ac)">verification</strong>, <strong style="color:var(--am)">quality</strong>, <strong style="color:var(--cy)">behavior</strong>, and the <strong>5-session arc</strong> where cost compounds. Numbers are tagged by provenance: [M] measured &middot; [C] computed &middot; [H] heuristic &middot; [X] external.</p>
-<div class="cards" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(160px,1fr))">
-<div class="card" style="text-align:center"><div class="cval" data-stat="stories_total">221</div><div class="cdesc" style="text-align:center">Multi-session stories</div></div>
-<div class="card" style="text-align:center"><div class="cval" data-stat="story_sessions">1,097</div><div class="cdesc" style="text-align:center">Sessions</div></div>
-<div class="card" style="text-align:center"><div class="cval" data-stat="variants">7</div><div class="cdesc" style="text-align:center">Models</div></div>
-<div class="card" style="text-align:center" title="[M] Sum of story session costs, verified against provider pricing"><div class="cval">$<span data-stat="story_total_cost">288.69</span></div><div class="cdesc" style="text-align:center">Total story cost</div></div>
+<!-- Hero: name the Golden Circle and establish both corpus boundaries before findings. -->
+<section class="sec golden-hero" style="padding-top:6rem">
+<div class="circle-label">SIMON SINEK'S GOLDEN CIRCLE · WHY / HOW / WHAT</div>
+<h1>The Evidence: WHY / HOW / WHAT</h1>
+<p class="lead" style="font-size:1rem;color:var(--t)"><strong>We began with an unmeasured gap:</strong> a passing result could not tell us how a model searched, recovered, verified, or changed the cost of the next session. We first built controlled single-session perturbation experiments to make search dynamics visible. Those experiments discovered the operators and recovery signals that the current multi-session story instrument reuses. What emerged is a field view of agentic work across cost, verification, quality, recovery, and time.</p>
+
+<div class="corpus-ledger" aria-label="Two-corpus evidence ledger">
+<article class="corpus-card precursor">
+<div class="corpus-status">ARCHIVED PRECURSOR · CHRONOLOGICALLY FIRST</div>
+<h2>Single-session perturbation corpus</h2>
+<p class="corpus-scope">Approximately 227 classified single-session runs tested controlled degradation. The relevant denominators remain separate: 224 game reports where report analysis applies and 201 Grit-matrix sessions where paired Grit analysis applies.</p>
+<div class="corpus-metrics">
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong>~227</strong>classified runs</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong>224</strong>game reports</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong>201</strong>Grit sessions</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong>8 × 10</strong>model variants × operators</div>
 </div>
+</article>
+<article class="corpus-card current">
+<div class="corpus-status">CURRENT INSTRUMENT · CHRONOLOGICALLY SECOND</div>
+<h2>Multi-session story corpus</h2>
+<p class="corpus-scope"><span data-stat="stories_total">221</span> executed stories comprise 210 unique cells plus 11 reruns across 3 codebases, 2 tiers, 2 codebase qualities, and the existing conditions. Their 5-session builds produced <span data-stat="story_sessions">1,097</span> sessions across <span data-stat="variants">7</span> models.</p>
+<div class="corpus-metrics">
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong data-stat="stories_total">221</strong>stories</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong data-stat="story_sessions">1,097</strong>sessions</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric"><strong data-stat="variants">7</strong>models</div>
+<div class="corpus-metric" title="[M] Sum of story session costs, verified against provider pricing"><strong>$<span data-stat="story_total_cost">288.69</span></strong>of $288.6909 total story cost</div>
+</div>
+</article>
+</div>
+<p class="corpus-boundary"><strong>These are two distinct measurements.</strong> The 227 single-session perturbation runs came first; the 1,097 story sessions came later and reuse the precursor's operators and recovery signals. They are presented together as a chronology, not merged into one denominator.</p>
 </section>

-<!-- ==================== LEGACY PERTURBATION PIPELINE ==================== -->
+<!-- WHY stays concise so the chronological evidence remains the center of the page. -->
+<section class="sec narrative-step">
+<div class="circle-label">WHY · THE CENTER</div>
+<h2 id="why-measure">WHY: The Gap a Passing Result Could Not Measure</h2>
+<p class="lead">A successful final output conceals the path that produced it. It does not reveal how degraded information changed the search, what recovery cost, how much verification the model chose, or whether today's output made tomorrow's task harder. The evidence page therefore begins with behavior under controlled stress, then follows the same signals into inherited, multi-session work.</p>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ==================== ARCHIVED PERTURBATION PRECURSOR ==================== -->
 <section class="sec" style="padding-top:4rem">
-<h2 id="perturbation">Legacy — Single-Session Perturbation Experiments</h2>
-<p class="lead" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--t3)">The sections below report the <em>earlier</em> perturbation pipeline — single-session experiments measuring search dynamics (basin escape, grit, recovery cost) under controlled specification degradation. These 227 runs generated the operators and recovery signals the story instrument now reuses, but they are a <strong>distinct, historical measurement</strong> from the multi-session story pipeline above. The story evidence is the current instrument; the perturbation results remain here for provenance. <a href="#story-models" style="color:var(--ac)">↑ Back to the story evidence.</a></p>
+<div class="circle-label">ACT I · HOW THE MEASUREMENT BEGAN</div>
+<h2 id="perturbation">Act I: Archived Precursor</h2>
+<p class="lead" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--t3)">The sections below report the <em>earlier</em> perturbation pipeline — single-session experiments measuring search dynamics (basin escape, grit, recovery cost) under controlled specification degradation. These 227 runs generated the operators and recovery signals the story instrument now reuses, but they are a <strong>distinct, historical measurement</strong> from the multi-session story pipeline that follows. The story evidence is the current instrument; the perturbation results remain here for provenance. <a href="#story-models" style="color:var(--ac)">Continue to the current story evidence ↓</a></p>
 </section>

